<article class="env-situation" id="0DIB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DIB">Situation <span data-tag="0DIB">38.29.1</span>.</a> Here we have an inverse system of rings $(A_ n)$ with surjective transition maps whose kernels are locally nilpotent. Set $A = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits A_ n$. We have a scheme $X$ proper, flat, and of finite presentation over $A$. We set $X_ n = X \times _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)} \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A_ n)$ and we view it as a closed subscheme of $X$. We assume further given a system $(K_ n, \varphi _ n)$ where $K_ n$ is a pseudo-coherent object of $D(\mathcal{O}_{X_ n})$ and </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \varphi _ n : K_ n \longrightarrow K_{n - 1}  \]
</div>
  <p> is a map in $D(\mathcal{O}_{X_ n})$ which induces an isomorphism $K_ n \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{X_ n}}^\mathbf {L} \mathcal{O}_{X_{n - 1}} \to K_{n - 1}$ in $D(\mathcal{O}_{X_{n - 1}})$. </p>
</article>